docs: rewrite README to match the clean-room shell; relicense to MIT

The previous README described the earlier feature-rich iteration (PTY
terminal, Review, Browser/Files, plugin marketplace, desktop skins, Pinned
Summary, and a built-in plugin table) — none of which exist in the current
codebase, which is a lean Electron shell + stock dsh web UI. Rewrite both
README.md and README.en.md to document what is actually implemented:

- architecture (Electron main + SidecarSupervisor + shared web profile)
- real menu/shortcuts (Cmd+N/O/B, Cmd+,,, Cmd+Shift+R)
- the @deepwork/desktop plugin's host/client faces
- accurate platform matrix and build/release flow
- an explicit note on features intentionally not included here

License: switch the project to MIT (LICENSE, package.json, notices,
badges).
